2026-09-10T07:03:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"message":"docs: add security policy","tree":{"sha":"b0aa132327affe902462b325b09276644f3ad8d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/b0aa132327affe902462b325b09276644f3ad8d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/02b49bd7c765ac52cd477be74ac71f4c30995890","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/02b49bd7c765ac52cd477be74ac71f4c30995890","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKDAyYjQ5YmQ3Yzc2NWFjNTJjZDQ3N2JlNzRhYzcxZjRjMzA5OTU4OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/e8cefaa15ac8363b2d6ea9219e3111a13405e56d","sha":"e8cefaa15ac8363b2d6ea9219e3111a13405e56d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/e8cefaa15ac8363b2d6ea9219e3111a13405e56d"}],"sha":"02b49bd7c765ac52cd477be74ac71f4c30995890","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/02b49bd7c765ac52cd477be74ac71f4c30995890"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/e8cefaa15ac8363b2d6ea9219e3111a13405e56d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:09Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:27:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: SUPPORT-646 coverage hardening (compute, permission-gate, retention, WCAG a11y) (#19)\n\n* test: add mockito-inline (4.11.0) for static and construction mocking\n\nEnables Mockito.mockStatic / mockConstruction (inline mock-maker), required to\nunit-test the code paths running inside the static\nJCRTemplate.doExecuteWithSystemSession(...) system session, the static\nFiles.createTempFile(...) call, and the Karaf command''s internally-constructed\ncomputer -- all without a live JCR repository. Test scope only; pinned to the\nmockito-core version. No production changes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover permission-gate guard, role XML, node-cap and multi-valued data\n\n- GraphQLPermissionGuardTest (F33): reflection guard asserting every top-level\n  @GraphQLField on JcrStatsQuery/JcrStatsMutation carries\n  @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"jcrStatsAdmin\") -- fails if a future field ships ungated.\n- RolesPermissionsXmlTest (F34): guards that roles.xml bundles administrationAccess +\n  jcrStatsAdmin with j:privilegedAccess, and permissions.xml defines admin/jcrStatsAdmin.\n- JcrStatsTraversalTest (U8, F4): multi-valued jcr:data contributes 0 size but is still\n  counted; the MAX_VISITED_NODES cap aborts with a documented error, not silent truncation.\n- JcrStatsServiceTest (U3): the never-cleared result cache serves run A''s tree while a\n  re-run is in flight (characterizes the documented stale-read hazard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover system-session paths and characterize exclusion divergence\n\nUses mockito-inline''s mockStatic to drive the real JcrStatsComputer callbacks against a\nmocked session inside JCRTemplate.doExecuteWithSystemSession, plus mockStatic(Files):\n- F35: computeStats routes through the privileged system session (ACL bypass) and aggregates.\n- U4/D2: saveSnapshot stores under a server-generated jcr-stats-<timestamp>.json name;\n  caller payload never names the file.\n- U5: >50 MB snapshot rejected before any JCR write; a just-under valid envelope is accepted.\n- U6/D1: the 51st snapshot prunes exactly the oldest (MAX_SNAPSHOTS=50); at cap, none pruned.\n- D5: an unwritable temp dir yields a null flamegraph while totals are still returned.\n- U2/D3 (ExclusionDivergenceTest): CHARACTERIZATION of the current divergence -- the 4-arg\n  computeStats honors exclusions, the 1-arg (size/nodeCount/tree/computeSize/CLI) ignores them.\n  Labeled for Stage-7 inversion once exclusions are made consistent.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover sync-read ACL bypass, reports/snapshots listing, and CLI command\n\n- JcrStatsQueryTest (U1): size/nodeCount/tree route through the privileged system session\n  (sync reads bypass read ACLs, still gated by @GraphQLRequiresPermission); -1 error sentinel.\n- JcrStatsQueryTest (U9): reports() SQL excludes the snapshots subfolder (NOT ISDESCENDANTNODE);\n  snapshots() sorts its folder listing by jcr:created descending in memory.\n- ComputeSizeCommandTest (F32): the Karaf command delegates the -p/-d options to\n  computeAndWriteFlamegraph and defaults to path=/ delete=false (via mockConstruction).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add WCAG 2.2 accessibility spec for the admin UI (F30)\n\nNew Cypress spec asserting the ARIA contract the React source ships: the progressbar''s\naria-valuemin/valuemax range while computing, role=status for success and role=alert for\nload errors, the flamegraph''s role=img + accessible name, accessible names on saved-execution\nrow buttons, focus not relocated to the flamegraph on async completion, and graceful behaviour\nunder prefers-reduced-motion. Mirrors the 02 spec harness (cy.login/apollo/waitUntil).\nLint/typecheck run in Stage 6 (tests/node_modules is not installed here).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): fix F30 flamegraph role=img assertion\n\nThe role=img + aria-label live on the flamegraph container element itself\n(data-testid=jcrstats-flamegraph-react), not on an ancestor. Assert the\nattributes on the element directly instead of via .parents(''[role=img]''),\nwhich never matched. Confirmed 7/7 green in the dockerized Cypress run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: apply configured path exclusions across all compute surfaces (D3/U2)\n\nPath exclusions were threaded into only the async compute() job; size,\nnodeCount, tree, computeSize and the Karaf CLI went through the single-arg\ncomputeStats overload (p -> false) and silently traversed/sized excluded\nsubtrees. Add JcrStatsComputer.liveExclusions() resolving the live config\npredicate, route every surface through it (computeAndWriteFlamegraph backs\nboth computeSize and the CLI), and reuse it in JcrStatsService.start (DRY).\n\nInvert ExclusionDivergenceTest from a divergence characterization into a\nconsistency invariant: with /root/big excluded every surface now returns\n100/2, plus a no-exclusions-configured guard proving byte-for-byte identical\n(600/4) behaviour when nothing is configured.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct snapshot retention, saveSnapshot signature, tmpdir and version\n\n- Snapshot retention is capped at 50 (MAX_SNAPSHOTS, oldest pruned on write),\n  not ''accumulate with no retention policy''.\n- saveSnapshot takes json (the full envelope); the filename is server-generated\n  jcr-stats-<timestamp>.json, not a caller-supplied name.\n- Flamegraph temp file uses java.io.tmpdir ($CATALINA_TMPDIR on Tomcat), not the\n  env var directly.\n- Align README/AGENTS version markers to the authoritative pom (2.1.4-SNAPSHOT).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"db77de2e613e747276449ef869c9228ebc1ccad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/db77de2e613e747276449ef869c9228ebc1ccad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/e8cefaa15ac8363b2d6ea9219e3111a13405e56d","verification":{"payload":"tree db77de2e613e747276449ef869c9228ebc1ccad2\nparent f3997ef0bc0f33bb3aff04e5158f2d01a8f6371f\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100429 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100429 +0200\n\ntest: SUPPORT-646 coverage hardening (compute, permission-gate, retention, WCAG a11y) (#19)\n\n* test: add mockito-inline (4.11.0) for static and construction mocking\n\nEnables Mockito.mockStatic / mockConstruction (inline mock-maker), required to\nunit-test the code paths running inside the static\nJCRTemplate.doExecuteWithSystemSession(...) system session, the static\nFiles.createTempFile(...) call, and the Karaf command''s internally-constructed\ncomputer -- all without a live JCR repository. Test scope only; pinned to the\nmockito-core version. No production changes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover permission-gate guard, role XML, node-cap and multi-valued data\n\n- GraphQLPermissionGuardTest (F33): reflection guard asserting every top-level\n  @GraphQLField on JcrStatsQuery/JcrStatsMutation carries\n  @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"jcrStatsAdmin\") -- fails if a future field ships ungated.\n- RolesPermissionsXmlTest (F34): guards that roles.xml bundles administrationAccess +\n  jcrStatsAdmin with j:privilegedAccess, and permissions.xml defines admin/jcrStatsAdmin.\n- JcrStatsTraversalTest (U8, F4): multi-valued jcr:data contributes 0 size but is still\n  counted; the MAX_VISITED_NODES cap aborts with a documented error, not silent truncation.\n- JcrStatsServiceTest (U3): the never-cleared result cache serves run A''s tree while a\n  re-run is in flight (characterizes the documented stale-read hazard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover system-session paths and characterize exclusion divergence\n\nUses mockito-inline''s mockStatic to drive the real JcrStatsComputer callbacks against a\nmocked session inside JCRTemplate.doExecuteWithSystemSession, plus mockStatic(Files):\n- F35: computeStats routes through the privileged system session (ACL bypass) and aggregates.\n- U4/D2: saveSnapshot stores under a server-generated jcr-stats-<timestamp>.json name;\n  caller payload never names the file.\n- U5: >50 MB snapshot rejected before any JCR write; a just-under valid envelope is accepted.\n- U6/D1: the 51st snapshot prunes exactly the oldest (MAX_SNAPSHOTS=50); at cap, none pruned.\n- D5: an unwritable temp dir yields a null flamegraph while totals are still returned.\n- U2/D3 (ExclusionDivergenceTest): CHARACTERIZATION of the current divergence -- the 4-arg\n  computeStats honors exclusions, the 1-arg (size/nodeCount/tree/computeSize/CLI) ignores them.\n  Labeled for Stage-7 inversion once exclusions are made consistent.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: cover sync-read ACL bypass, reports/snapshots listing, and CLI command\n\n- JcrStatsQueryTest (U1): size/nodeCount/tree route through the privileged system session\n  (sync reads bypass read ACLs, still gated by @GraphQLRequiresPermission); -1 error sentinel.\n- JcrStatsQueryTest (U9): reports() SQL excludes the snapshots subfolder (NOT ISDESCENDANTNODE);\n  snapshots() sorts its folder listing by jcr:created descending in memory.\n- ComputeSizeCommandTest (F32): the Karaf command delegates the -p/-d options to\n  computeAndWriteFlamegraph and defaults to path=/ delete=false (via mockConstruction).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): add WCAG 2.2 accessibility spec for the admin UI (F30)\n\nNew Cypress spec asserting the ARIA contract the React source ships: the progressbar''s\naria-valuemin/valuemax range while computing, role=status for success and role=alert for\nload errors, the flamegraph''s role=img + accessible name, accessible names on saved-execution\nrow buttons, focus not relocated to the flamegraph on async completion, and graceful behaviour\nunder prefers-reduced-motion. Mirrors the 02 spec harness (cy.login/apollo/waitUntil).\nLint/typecheck run in Stage 6 (tests/node_modules is not installed here).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(e2e): fix F30 flamegraph role=img assertion\n\nThe role=img + aria-label live on the flamegraph container element itself\n(data-testid=jcrstats-flamegraph-react), not on an ancestor. Assert the\nattributes on the element directly instead of via .parents(''[role=img]''),\nwhich never matched. Confirmed 7/7 green in the dockerized Cypress run.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: apply configured path exclusions across all compute surfaces (D3/U2)\n\nPath exclusions were threaded into only the async compute() job; size,\nnodeCount, tree, computeSize and the Karaf CLI went through the single-arg\ncomputeStats overload (p -> false) and silently traversed/sized excluded\nsubtrees. Add JcrStatsComputer.liveExclusions() resolving the live config\npredicate, route every surface through it (computeAndWriteFlamegraph backs\nboth computeSize and the CLI), and reuse it in JcrStatsService.start (DRY).\n\nInvert ExclusionDivergenceTest from a divergence characterization into a\nconsistency invariant: with /root/big excluded every surface now returns\n100/2, plus a no-exclusions-configured guard proving byte-for-byte identical\n(600/4) behaviour when nothing is configured.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* docs: correct snapshot retention, saveSnapshot signature, tmpdir and version\n\n- Snapshot retention is capped at 50 (MAX_SNAPSHOTS, oldest pruned on write),\n  not ''accumulate with no retention policy''.\n- saveSnapshot takes json (the full envelope); the filename is server-generated\n  jcr-stats-<timestamp>.json, not a caller-supplied name.\n- Flamegraph temp file uses java.io.tmpdir ($CATALINA_TMPDIR on Tomcat), not the\n  env var directly.\n- Align README/AGENTS version markers to the authoritative pom (2.1.4-SNAPSHOT).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzZNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYvQQADyDpo5Q3N7G0cScdIFclUMk\n1C+lvXiT9Cue4XpxQZqcWjMPM5kJlwk7h4TXX6bWkz9qmhqJ211pzyWayVXxghOn\nwOVlLMI7kSXc4DK37lWuQqWVi9UTeqP37HBI7iDI+JQSgfX7CYpgUn5qdBeMdaMy\nDNlr81COIYdLSJ0CccZ6LcEfHbVRxBO6cd57dGnP9eNWZznCaM/Qv47x9/fBIMUc\n1g76lFvyg4Q5vHW9UiADt/KWR7lFUdTzYtlo9oyyanJcHbiEDDW/sCVuNydZjc3p\n0