d35idoAKDk1MzM5YzUxMTdiYjZhYTQ3NzA1ZDkxZjMzOGM4NDRlMjZlYTgxMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/bbf9759d3d36b336274763197864cef3d3879a0a","sha":"bbf9759d3d36b336274763197864cef3d3879a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/bbf9759d3d36b336274763197864cef3d3879a0a"}],"sha":"95339c5117bb6aa47705d91f338c844e26ea810c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/95339c5117bb6aa47705d91f338c844e26ea810c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/bbf9759d3d36b336274763197864cef3d3879a0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T16:21:25Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T16:21:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: admin page vertical scroll + Saved executions above View (#10)\n\n* fix: add vertical scroll to admin page when content exceeds the frame\n\nThe Jahia admin (moonstone) settings frame is a fixed-height, overflow:hidden\nregion, so each route must own its own scrolling. The .js_container route root\nset width/padding but no height/overflow, so once the results, flamegraph and\nSaved-executions/Exclusions panels stacked taller than the frame the bottom was\nclipped with no scrollbar. Make the container fill the frame and scroll its own\noverflow (border-box keeps the 24px padding inside the scroll box).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: move Saved executions section above the View (results) section\n\nThe run-history panel now renders above the results/View section instead of\nbelow it, so saved executions are the first thing reached after the controls.\nSnapshotsPanel still returns null when empty, so it adds no vertical space until\na run has been saved. Exclusions stays below results (short-viewport guard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: update flamegraph viewport test for scroll + reorder contract\n\nMoving Saved executions above the View section pushes the flamegraph down, so on\nthe 1366x768 test viewport its auto-sized height hits the MIN_HEIGHT floor and the\nbottom extends past the window. That is intentional now that the route container\nowns a vertical scrollbar (nothing is clipped). Replace the obsolete ''fits the\nviewport'' assertion with full-width + usable-height checks and assert the route\ncontainer is a vertical scroll container. Adds data-testid=jcrstats-container.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"7dac02b2c58a13e9baf5a59ccbe8fc2fe8d94f31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/7dac02b2c58a13e9baf5a59ccbe8fc2fe8d94f31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/bbf9759d3d36b336274763197864cef3d3879a0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7dac02b2c58a13e9baf5a59ccbe8fc2fe8d94f31\nparent b323eeeb166511b9eedf9362a5c3d3e5765de292\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782404485 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782404485 +0200\n\nfix: admin page vertical scroll + Saved executions above View (#10)\n\n* fix: add vertical scroll to admin page when content exceeds the frame\n\nThe Jahia admin (moonstone) settings frame is a fixed-height, overflow:hidden\nregion, so each route must own its own scrolling. The .js_container route root\nset width/padding but no height/overflow, so once the results, flamegraph and\nSaved-executions/Exclusions panels stacked taller than the frame the bottom was\nclipped with no scrollbar. Make the container fill the frame and scroll its own\noverflow (border-box keeps the 24px padding inside the scroll box).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: move Saved executions section above the View (results) section\n\nThe run-history panel now renders above the results/View section instead of\nbelow it, so saved executions are the first thing reached after the controls.\nSnapshotsPanel still returns null when empty, so it adds no vertical space until\na run has been saved. Exclusions stays below results (short-viewport guard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: update flamegraph viewport test for scroll + reorder contract\n\nMoving Saved executions above the View section pushes the flamegraph down, so on\nthe 1366x768 test viewport its auto-sized height hits the MIN_HEIGHT floor and the\nbottom extends past the window. That is intentional now that the route container\nowns a vertical scrollbar (nothing is clipped). Replace the obsolete ''fits the\nviewport'' assertion with full-width + usable-height checks and assert the route\ncontainer is a vertical scroll container. Adds data-testid=jcrstats-container.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPV