a/jcr-stats/commit/f4b3ffd74e6d2b8cc03105747569601b9f281565","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKGY0YjNmZmQ3NGU2ZDJiOGNjMDMxMDU3NDc1Njk2MDFiOWYyODE1NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/acd14a16e9924c0961108023ad4ed0250ef1465b","sha":"acd14a16e9924c0961108023ad4ed0250ef1465b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/acd14a16e9924c0961108023ad4ed0250ef1465b"}],"sha":"f4b3ffd74e6d2b8cc03105747569601b9f281565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/f4b3ffd74e6d2b8cc03105747569601b9f281565"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/acd14a16e9924c0961108023ad4ed0250ef1465b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T15:30:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T15:30:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: whole-site traversal usability — recover, cancel, exclude paths, saved executions (2.1.2) (#9)\n\n* fix: skip un-listable branches instead of aborting whole-site traversal\n\nWalking a subtree that descends into an external data-source mount whose\nchild names are not valid JCR paths (e.g. cloud-dumps nodes named with an\nISO-8601 timestamp, where '':'' is the namespace-prefix separator) raised\n''RepositoryException: Invalid path ... not valid name character'' from\nnode.getNodes() and aborted the entire computation.\n\nMake traversal best-effort: log a WARN and skip an un-enumerable node or a\nsingle failing child rather than failing the whole job. The hard\nMAX_VISITED_NODES limit still aborts, via a dedicated TraversalLimitException\nthat the per-branch handlers re-throw. Adds two regression tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: recover valid children via escaped query when direct listing fails\n\nSupersedes the skip-only approach: when the eager node.getNodes() listing\nthrows on an invalid JCR child name (external-provider node named with an\nISO-8601 timestamp, '':'' = namespace-prefix separator), fall back to an\nISCHILDNODE query whose path is escaped via JCRContentUtils.sqlEncode. The\nindex returns the valid children (the un-representable node is absent), so the\nrest of the branch is recovered instead of dropped. Skip only if the escaped\nquery also fails. MAX_VISITED_NODES still aborts via TraversalLimitException.\nTargets 2.1.2 (2.1.1 already released); CHANGELOG moved accordingly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: real server-side cancellation of the async computation\n\nThe Cancel button previously only stopped client-side polling; the server\njob kept running to completion. Add cooperative cancellation: the traversal\npolls an AtomicBoolean (via a BooleanSupplier threaded into computeNode) at\nthe start of every node and aborts between nodes (never mid-JCR-operation)\nthrough a CancelledException the per-branch handlers re-throw.\n\nWiring: JcrStatsService.cancel() sets the flag and is exposed as the\njcrStats.cancel GraphQL mutation; jcrStats.status gains a ''cancelled'' flag so\nthe UI distinguishes a cancelled stop from an error. The Cancel button now\ncalls the mutation; the poll treats status.cancelled as a clean stop.\nAdds a cancel unit test and updates status carrier tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: exclude paths from the computation, persisted in an OSGi config file\n\nAdds the ability to exclude JCR paths (a path and its whole subtree are\nskipped) from size computations.\n\n- JcrStatsConfig: a ManagedService (PID org.jahia.community.jcrstats) holding\n  the excluded set; UI edits are written to ${karaf.etc}/<pid>.cfg atomically\n  (temp + ATOMIC_MOVE, property jcrStats.excludedPaths) and round-trip back via\n  updated(), so they survive restarts and can be hand-edited.\n- Traversal: computeNode skips any child the excluded predicate matches (threaded\n  in via computeStats, alongside the cancellation flag).\n- GraphQL: jcrStats.exclusions (query), addExclusion/removeExclusion (mutations).\n- UI: ''Exclude this path'' on the focused flamegraph frame + an Excluded-paths\n  list with Remove; exclusions apply on the next compute.\n\nAdds JcrStatsConfigTest (parse/validate/match + real temp-dir persistence\nround-trip) and a traversal exclusion test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: auto-save each execution as a JSON snapshot in the JCR for later viewing\n\nEvery completed async computation is now serialized to a timestamped JSON file\nunder /sites/systemsite/files/jcr-stats/snapshots/, so a past run''s flamegraph\ncan be reopened later (and survives restarts), by anyone with jcrStatsAdmin.\n\n- JcrStatsComputer.writeJsonSnapshot builds the same export envelope as the UI\n  Save/Load (format jcr-stats-flamegraph, depth-limited tree) and uploads it as\n  a jnt:file; buildSnapshotJson/jsonEscape are package-private for unit testing.\n- JcrStatsService writes the snapshot on successful completion only.\n- GraphQL jcrStats.snapshots lists them (most recent first); reports() now\n  excludes the snapshots subfolder so HTML reports and JSON stay separate.\n- UI: a ''Saved executions'' panel lists snapshots with a View action that fetches\n  the stored JSON and loads it through the existing validated importer.\n\nAdds jsonEscape/buildSnapshotJson tests (70 Java tests; FE lint clean, 84 jest).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: compare two saved executions via the snapshot history\n\nAdd a Compare action next to View on each saved execution. View loads a\nsnapshot as the current tree; Compare loads another as the diff baseline, so\ntwo stored computations are diffed in the existing Comparison view (DiffTable).\nuseSnapshotLoader now shares a fetch+extractTree step and returns both\nhandlers. FE lint clean, 84 jest tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: Load data persists as a saved execution; remove standalone Compare-with\n\nNow that runs are stored server-side, unify the data store: loading a JSON file\nalso saves it as a server snapshot (new jcrStats.saveSnapshot mutation), so it\njoins the Saved executions history. The standalone ''Compare with...'' button and\nits baseline file upload are removed — comparison is driven from the Saved\nexecutions list (View one run, Compare another). Diff machinery unchanged.\n\nJcrStatsComputer.saveSnapshot validates size + envelope and reuses storeSnapshot;\nsnapshot filenames now include millis so same-second saves don''t collide.\n70 Java tests, 84 jest, ESLint clean, full build green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional blind review\n\nBlind review across architecture, security, code quality (SonarQube + lint),\nergonomy, accessibility (AAA), test coverage and documentation, then fixes by\narea:\n\nSecurity/correctness: snapshot & flamegraph writes use a dedicated system\nsession (JCRTemplate) instead of getCurrentSystemSession; saveSnapshot now\nvalidates the envelope structurally (org.json) instead of a substring match;\ndeleteSnapshot is restricted to the snapshots folder; cancellation is\nclassified by exception type; flamegraph write aborts on header/footer failure;\njsonEscape escapes lone surrogates; jcr:data read guards multi-valued props;\nexcluded-path validation hardened (length cap, linear checks — no ReDoS regex).\n\nCode quality: SonarQube quality gate green (S135/S107/S125 fixed, S1075\nsuppressed on the JCR content path); yarn lint clean. Fixed a stale-status race\nthat could apply a previous run''s result to a new run; scoped snapshot refetch\nto successful runs; surfaced load-as-snapshot failures.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): no focus relocation on async completion; reduced\nmotion fully stops the progress animation; role=status for info/success;\ndescriptive button names; flamegraph role=img; progressbar valuemin/max; AAA\ncontrast; heading reflow.\n\nErgonomy: saved-executions show date/size + per-row Delete; snapshot retention\ncap (50); Compare gated on a current result.\n\nDocs: README/AGENTS updated to 2.1.2 (exclusions, cancellation, snapshots, the\n.cfg config, route-name fix); package.json version synced.\n\nTests: 87 Java + 106 JS; added backend (saveSnapshot/cancel/jsonEscape/\nbuildSnapshotJson/exclusions/escaped-query fallback) and frontend controller\ntests; new Cypress specs for cancel/snapshot/exclusion flows.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings\n\n- pruneOldSnapshots re-fetches the snapshots folder fresh (no stale pre-save()\n  node reference); still best-effort inside the system session.\n- isValidPath rejects ''.''/''..'' only as whole path segments, so legitimate node\n  names like /sites/my..site/files are no longer wrongly rejected.\n- Exclusion add/remove failures now show dedicated errorExclude/errorUnexclude\n  messages instead of the misleading ''computation failed''.\n- Loading a file no longer flashes a success banner before a possible save\n  failure: the status is set only once the save resolves.\n- Cancellation test asserts the CancelledException type (the real contract),\n  not the message string; removed a dead i18n key.\n\n88 Java + 107 JS tests pass; SonarQube gate OK; lint clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: final AAA accessibility gaps + doc nits from loop-2 review\n\n- Compare (saved executions) is no longer a disabled button (which dropped it\n  from keyboard/AT focus order so users couldn''t learn why it was unavailable);\n  it stays operable and, when no current result is loaded, announces an info\n  message explaining the requirement instead.\n- Replaced the inaccessible window.confirm delete guard with an accessible\n  inline two-step confirm (Confirm/Cancel buttons, focus moved to Confirm,\n  descriptive names) — no native dialog, not silently skipped.\n- Docs: MAX_DEPTH coupling note now lists all four locations and points at\n  jcrStatsController.js (where the FE constant now lives).\n\n88 Java + 108 JS tests; lint clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix Cypress E2E specs against the renamed admin route + inline delete confirm\n\n- adminPath/ADMIN_PATH were still ''/jahia/administration/jcrStatsExecution'';\n  the route was renamed to ''jcrStats'' when the admin menu was merged, so every\n  cy.visit() hit a dead URL and the whole suite failed to load the component.\n- The delete-snapshot test still drove the old window.confirm; updated it to the\n  accessible inline two-step confirm (Delete arms the row, then the\n  jcrstats-snapshot-confirm-delete button performs it).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: flamegraph re-measure on panel render + harden cancel/delete E2E\n\nFrom running the Cypress suite (31/33 → fixing the last 2 in 02-jcrStatsAdmin):\n- Component: re-measure the flamegraph when the Exclusions/Saved-executions\n  panels appear or change (they render above the results and the snapshots panel\n  arrives async), so the graph no longer keeps a stale height and overflow past\n  the viewport bottom (fixes the viewport-sizing E2E).\n- Cancel E2E: wait for the progress block to render, click Cancel inside it, and\n  assert the progress block disappears — no longer races a fast job.\n- Delete E2E: use a retrying length assertion (the list re-renders only after the\n  post-delete refetch) instead of a one-shot DOM read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: list snapshots via direct child iteration + cap panel height\n\nResolves the last two E2E failures, both real product issues:\n- snapshots() listed via an ISDESCENDANTNODE Lucene query, which lags behind a\n  node deletion, so a just-deleted snapshot kept showing until the index caught\n  up. List the snapshots folder''s children directly (sorted by jcr:created desc)\n  for immediate consistency after delete — same rationale as the traversal fix.\n- The Exclusions/Saved-executions list now has a capped height with internal\n  scroll, so a long history no longer grows the page and pushes the flamegraph\n  past the viewport bottom (also a real unbounded-growth ergonomy fix).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: render exclusions/snapshots panels below results; settle delete E2E\n\nClean-room Cypress (Docker harness) showed the last 2 failures are real:\n- Viewport: the Exclusions/Saved-executions panels rendered ABOVE the results\n  consumed vertical space, and with the flamegraph''s MIN_HEIGHT floor the graph\n  overflowed the viewport bottom on a 768px-tall window. Move both panels BELOW\n  the results so the flamegraph''s top (and fit) matches the original layout.\n- Delete E2E: the loaded file is auto-saved asynchronously, so the row count\n  could increment right after rowsBefore was captured (net zero after delete).\n  Wait for the ''saved to history'' success banner before counting.\nReverted the now-moot measure() re-trigger on panel changes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0f6ff83c26cb1fb37dc901cf25e3c30881298b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/c0f6ff83c26cb1fb37dc901cf25e3c30881298b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/acd14a16e9924c0961108023ad4ed0250ef1465b","verification":{"payload":"tree c0f6ff83c26cb1fb37dc901cf25e3c30881298b4\nparent 8e4750f842ab2e20d18e36a9a6cd33173dbb71f0\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782401407 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782401407 +0200\n\nfeat: whole-site traversal usability — recover, cancel, exclude paths, saved executions (2.1.2) (#9)\n\n* fix: skip un-listable branches instead of aborting whole-site traversal\n\nWalking a subtree that descends into an external data-source mount whose\nchild names are not valid JCR paths (e.g. cloud-dumps nodes named with an\nISO-8601 timestamp, where '':'' is the namespace-prefix separator) raised\n''RepositoryException: Invalid path ... not valid name character'' from\nnode.getNodes() and aborted the entire computation.\n\nMake traversal best-effort: log a WARN and skip an un-enumerable node or a\nsingle failing child rather than failing the whole job. The hard\nMAX_VISITED_NODES limit still aborts, via a dedicated TraversalLimitException\nthat the per-branch handlers re-throw. Adds two regression tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: recover valid children via escaped query when direct listing fails\n\nSupersedes the skip-only approach: when the eager node.getNodes() listing\nthrows on an invalid JCR child name (external-provider node named with an\nISO-8601 timestamp, '':'' = namespace-prefix separator), fall back to an\nISCHILDNODE query whose path is escaped via JCRContentUtils.sqlEncode. The\nindex returns the valid children (the un-representable node is absent), so the\nrest of the branch is recovered instead of dropped. Skip only if the escaped\nquery also fails. MAX_VISITED_NODES still aborts via TraversalLimitException.\nTargets 2.1.2 (2.1.1 already released); CHANGELOG moved accordingly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: real server-side cancellation of the async computation\n\nThe Cancel button previously only stopped client-side polling; the server\njob kept running to completion. Add cooperative cancellation: the traversal\npolls an AtomicBoolean (via a BooleanSupplier threaded into computeNode) at\nthe start of every node and aborts between nodes (never mid-JCR-operation)\nthrough a CancelledException the per-branch handlers re-throw.\n\nWiring: JcrStatsService.cancel() sets the flag and is exposed as the\njcrStats.cancel GraphQL mutation; jcrStats.status gains a ''cancelled'' flag so\nthe UI distinguishes a cancelled stop from an error. The Cancel button now\ncalls the mutation; the poll treats status.cancelled as a clean stop.\nAdds a cancel unit test and updates status carrier tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: exclude paths from the computation, persisted in an OSGi config file\n\nAdds the ability to exclude JCR paths (a path and its whole subtree are\nskipped) from size computations.\n\n- JcrStatsConfig: a ManagedService (PID org.jahia.community.jcrstats) holding\n  the excluded set; UI edits are written to ${karaf.etc}/<pid>.cfg atomically\n  (temp + ATOMIC_MOVE, property jcrStats.excludedPaths) and round-trip back via\n  updated(), so they survive restarts and can be hand-edited.\n- Traversal: computeNode skips any child the excluded predicate matches (threaded\n  in via computeStats, alongside the cancellation flag).\n- GraphQL: jcrStats.exclusions (query), addExclusion/removeExclusion (mutations).\n- UI: ''Exclude this path'' on the focused flamegraph frame + an Excluded-paths\n  list with Remove; exclusions apply on the next compute.\n\nAdds JcrStatsConfigTest (parse/validate/match + real temp-dir persistence\nround-trip) and a traversal exclusion test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: auto-save each execution as a JSON snapshot in the JCR for later viewing\n\nEvery completed async computation is now serialized to a timestamped JSON file\nunder /sites/systemsite/files/jcr-stats/snapshots/, so a past run''s flamegraph\ncan be reopened later (and survives restarts), by anyone with jcrStatsAdmin.\n\n- JcrStatsComputer.writeJsonSnapshot builds the same export envelope as the UI\n  Save/Load (format jcr-stats-flamegraph, depth-limited tree) and uploads it as\n  a jnt:file; buildSnapshotJson/jsonEscape are package-private for unit testing.\n- JcrStatsService writes the snapshot on successful completion only.\n- GraphQL jcrStats.snapshots lists them (most recent first); reports() now\n  excludes the snapshots subfolder so HTML reports and JSON stay separate.\n- UI: a ''Saved executions'' panel lists snapshots with a View action that fetches\n  the stored JSON and loads it through the existing validated importer.\n\nAdds jsonEscape/buildSnapshotJson tests (70 Java tests; FE lint clean, 84 jest).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: compare two saved executions via the snapshot history\n\nAdd a Compare action next to View on each saved execution. View loads a\nsnapshot as the current tree; Compare loads another as the diff baseline, so\ntwo stored computations are diffed in the existing Comparison view (DiffTable).\nuseSnapshotLoader now shares a fetch+extractTree step and returns both\nhandlers. FE lint clean, 84 jest tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: Load data persists as a saved execution; remove standalone Compare-with\n\nNow that runs are stored server-side, unify the data store: loading a JSON file\nalso saves it as a server snapshot (new jcrStats.saveSnapshot mutation), so it\njoins the Saved executions history. The standalone ''Compare with...'' button and\nits baseline file upload are removed — comparison is driven from the Saved\nexecutions list (View one run, Compare another). Diff machinery unchanged.\n\nJcrStatsComputer.saveSnapshot validates size + envelope and reuses storeSnapshot;\nsnapshot filenames now include millis so same-second saves don''t collide.\n70 Java tests, 84 jest, ESLint clean, full build green.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional blind review\n\nBlind review across architecture, security, code quality (SonarQube + lint),\nergonomy, accessibility (AAA), test coverage and documentation, then fixes by\narea:\n\nSecurity/correctness: snapshot & flamegraph writes use a dedicated system\nsession (JCRTemplate) instead of getCurrentSystemSession; saveSnapshot now\nvalidates the envelope structurally (org.json) instead of a substring match;\ndeleteSnapshot is restricted to the snapshots folder; cancellation is\nclassified by exception type; flamegraph write aborts on header/footer failure;\njsonEscape escapes lone surrogates; jcr:data read guards multi-valued props;\nexcluded-path validation hardened (length cap, linear checks — no ReDoS regex).\n\nCode quality: SonarQube quality gate green (S135/S107/S125 fixed, S1075\nsuppressed on the JCR content path); yarn lint clean. Fixed a stale-status race\nthat could apply a previous run''s result to a new run; scoped snapshot refetch\nto successful runs; surfaced load-as-snapshot failures.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): no focus relocation on async completion; reduced\nmotion fully stops the progress animation; role=status for info/success;\ndescriptive button names; flamegraph role=img; progressbar valuemin/max; AAA\ncontrast; heading reflow.\n\nErgonomy: saved-executions show date/size + per-row Delete; snapshot retention\ncap (50); Compare gated on a current result.\n\nDocs: README/AGENTS updated to 2.1.2 (exclusions, cancellation, snapshots, the\n.cfg config, route-name fix); package.json version synced.\n\nTests: 87 Java + 106 JS; added backend (saveSnapshot/cancel/jsonEscape/\nbuildSnapshotJson/exclusions/escaped-query fallback) and frontend controller\ntests; new Cypress specs for cancel/snapshot/exclusion flows.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR blind-review findings\n\n- pruneOldSnapshots re-fetches the snapshots folder fresh (no stale pre-save()\n  node reference); still best-effort inside the system session.\n- isValidPath rejects ''.''/''..'' only as whole path segments, so legitimate node\n  names like /sites/my..site/files are no longer wrongly rejected.\n- Exclusion add/remove failures now show dedicated errorExclude/errorUnexclude\n  messages instead of the misleading ''computation failed''.\n- Loading a file no longer flashes a success banner before a possible save\n  failure: the status is set only once the save resolves.\n- Cancellation test asserts the CancelledException type (the real contract),\n  not the message string; removed a dead i18n key.\n\n88 Java + 107 JS tests pass; SonarQube gate OK; lint clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: final AAA accessibility gaps + doc nits from loop-2 review\n\n- Compare (saved executions) is no longer a disabled button (which dropped it\n  from keyboard/AT focus order so users couldn''t learn why it was unavailable);\n  it stays operable and, when no current result is loaded, announces an info\n  message explaining the requirement instead.\n- Replaced the inaccessible window.confirm delete guard with an accessible\n  inline two-step confirm (Confirm/Cancel buttons, focus moved to Confirm,\n  descriptive names) — no native dialog, not silently skipped.\n- Docs: MAX_DEPTH coupling note now lists all four locations and points at\n  jcrStatsController.js (where the FE constant now lives).\n\n88 Java + 108 JS tests; lint clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix Cypress E2E specs against the renamed admin route + inline delete confirm\n\n- adminPath/ADMIN_PATH were still ''/jahia/administration/jcrStatsExecution'';\n  the route was renamed to ''jcrStats'' when the admin menu was merged, so every\n  cy.visit() hit a dead URL and the whole suite failed to load the component.\n- The delete-snapshot test still drove the old window.confirm; updated it to the\n  accessible inline two-step confirm (Delete arms the row, then the\n  jcrstats-snapshot-confirm-delete button performs it).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: flamegraph re-measure on panel render + harden cancel/delete E2E\n\nFrom running the Cypress suite (31/33 → fixing the last 2 in 02-jcrStatsAdmin):\n- Component: re-measure the flamegraph when the Exclusions/Saved-executions\n  panels appear or change (they render above the results and the snapshots panel\n  arrives async), so the graph no longer keeps a stale height and overflow past\n  the viewport bottom (fixes the viewport-sizing E2E).\n- Cancel E2E: wait for the progress block to render, click Cancel inside it, and\n  assert the progress block disappears — no longer races a fast job.\n- Delete E2E: use a retrying length assertion (the list re-renders only after the\n  post-delete refetch) instead of a one-shot DOM read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: list snapshots via direct child iteration + cap panel height\n\nResolves the last two E2E failures, both real product issues:\n- snapshots() listed via an ISDESCENDANTNODE Lucene query, which lags behind a\n  node deletion, so a just-deleted snapshot kept showing until the index caught\n  up. List the snapshots folder''s children directly (sorted by jcr:created desc)\n  for immediate consistency after delete — same rationale as the traversal fix.\n- The Exclusions/Saved-executions list now has a capped height with internal\n  scroll, so a long history no longer grows the page and pushes the flamegraph\n  past the viewport bottom (also a real unbounded-growth ergonomy fix).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: render exclusions/snapshots panels below results; settle delete E2E\n\nClean-room Cypress (Docker harness) showed the last 2 failures are real:\n- Viewport: the Exclusions/Saved-executions panels rendered ABOVE the results\n  consumed vertical space, and with the flamegraph''s MIN_HEIGHT floor the graph\n  overflowed the viewport bottom on a 768px-tall window. Move both panels BELOW\n  the results so the flamegraph''s top (and fit) matches the original layout.\n- Delete E2E: the loaded file is auto-saved asynchronously, so the row count\n  could increment right after rowsBefore was captured (net zero after delete).\n  Wait for the ''saved to history'' success banner before counting.\nReverted the now-moot measure() re-trigger on panel changes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPUl/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACkYQAC/Y13fstkk3IMEZOiV2TQrT\nMmH4NTfR5ju4NSusuvqRyRMpIyIIARrI7RJbdIWF8AVWxmUyo6Md1z74mU0cZmgd\nklOoJylVvAGBFbmUSmRuX7AQJs2ZuVovlZo9dtRddTrEWkNFR6P6qPK93oSmxSHL\ntqBti014o1AYVHggCOSl8s6IoNVixcLoWA9FOoYG30ocW8rpTtgiym+XWuOUC4YW\ntCPeDv95PU2QsM/h9mt/NdPWbUGlivo8k4naljCefn1dr1z0VsM3980P8Sqf/gJX\niAMnsqrAwZKd+ygVjXtWgcfoNb8aYv9Q/+VJlUX52fCUo/eO4o3ymHM6RFxIAMjk\nNcjts9slcVq1O4rCWA2Zx4K1CYpQN6553YhTHG3XErdwK3TbyS2kujMw6MImN6u2\n6+CcVIqnMsr/8IkMbo6eOPBVtZHW6sf6XiqvLOYoLeqLmp42YRSststIRWEQKL2M\n/i327K6eSTZguQNWRAF29xK34itPuG2oREYSMrTMp1oV79KOOY/l+VPsLgS+ZvHG\n49LM7DSEt8Cb0NxAj/PUCKQlbJFGBhnTyP7vR5vm3phl2rHIPkggAiY1zW2QJB4b\nU32ACxUnyQqVRBWdy+tZoprf50CXYAbzQeoeRTIjwfbb8T3y/np3oiKW9FJcSNh4\ng07zS