ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/d71ce4fe09e88584c04f0aeba35b2fe9b05dca7b","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKGQ3MWNlNGZlMDllODg1ODRjMDRmMGFlYmEzNWIyZmU5YjA1ZGNhN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d","sha":"5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d"}],"sha":"d71ce4fe09e88584c04f0aeba35b2fe9b05dca7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/d71ce4fe09e88584c04f0aeba35b2fe9b05dca7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:37:15Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:37:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional review (security, a11y AAA, async race, Sonar gate, coverage) (#6)\n\n* fix: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional review (security, a11y AAA, async race, Sonar gate, coverage)\n\nBlind review across architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy, accessibility,\ntest coverage and documentation, then applied targeted fixes.\n\nBackend (Java):\n- S3077: publish lastResult via AtomicReference; build executor once in a final field (no volatile on a mutable type)\n- S2629: evaluate the byte-size display string outside LOGGER.info\n- S1905: drop redundant int casts in jsEscape (compare char literals)\n- NodeStats.getSubNodeStats() returns an unmodifiable set\n- defensive MAX_VISITED_NODES traversal cap to bound OOM/DoS on over-broad paths\n- sqlEncode the reports() JCR-SQL2 query for defense-in-depth\n- jacoco-maven-plugin + sonar coverage report paths\n\nFrontend (React):\n- fix async result race: gate cancellation on real unmount, not the computing-flip teardown\n- remove console.debug; log swallowed errors\n- cancel affordance + client poll timeout; block blank-path full-repo traversal\n- distinct, actionable error/success messages\n- harden snapshot import (size/depth/node caps, finite numbers, prototype-pollution keys)\n- DRY JContentLink component\n- AAA: focus-visible, 44px targets, contrast >=7:1, progress live region + aria-valuetext, reduced-motion tick\n- jest --coverage + lcov; new extractTree/toFlameNode/table tests\n\nTests: jsEscape, JcrStatsService gate/elapsed, data-carrier getters.\nDocs: document the async API + progress/resume; correct the system-session ACL claim; add Known Limitations.\n\nQuality gate OK (0 open issues, coverage 0->39%); 28/28 Cypress E2E green; 52 Java + 84 JS unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (no-result feedback, unmount guard, traversal cap off-by-one)\n\n- JcrStats.jsx: surface an error message when the server finishes with no result\n  (was a silent blank UI); guard the polling effect against unmount; restore an\n  explicit null guard in readFile before the onTree callback.\n- jcrStatsUtils.js: validateNode depth check uses >= so the enforced limit matches\n  MAX_IMPORT_DEPTH exactly.\n- JcrStatsComputer.java: MAX_VISITED_NODES check uses >= to honor the stated cap.\n- JcrStatsService.java: drop the dead null check in deactivate() (executor is final).\n\n28/28 Cypress E2E green; 52 Java + 84 JS unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): link text contrast to AAA 7:1 (#006fa0 -> #005a82)\n\nFinal-pass WCAG 2.2 AAA review: the \"Open in jContent\" link text used #006fa0\n(~5.9:1 on white — AA only). Darkened to #005a82 (~7.1:1) to meet SC 1.4.6.\nThe description left-border keeps #006fa0 (non-text UI boundary, SC 1.4.11 needs only 3:1);\ncomments corrected to reflect the right thresholds.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d40de9657b8167ed012ecd18c39482dcc6f9dd74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/d40de9657b8167ed012ecd18c39482dcc6f9dd74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d","verification":{"payload":"tree d40de9657b8167ed012ecd18c39482dcc6f9dd74\nparent 4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782149835 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782149835 +0200\n\nfix: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional review (security, a11y AAA, async race, Sonar gate, coverage) (#6)\n\n* fix: harden jcr-stats after multi-dimensional review (security, a11y AAA, async race, Sonar gate, coverage)\n\nBlind review across architecture, security, code quality, ergonomy, accessibility,\ntest coverage and documentation, then applied targeted fixes.\n\nBackend (Java):\n- S3077: publish lastResult via AtomicReference; build executor once in a final field (no volatile on a mutable type)\n- S2629: evaluate the byte-size display string outside LOGGER.info\n- S1905: drop redundant int casts in jsEscape (compare char literals)\n- NodeStats.getSubNodeStats() returns an unmodifiable set\n- defensive MAX_VISITED_NODES traversal cap to bound OOM/DoS on over-broad paths\n- sqlEncode the reports() JCR-SQL2 query for defense-in-depth\n- jacoco-maven-plugin + sonar coverage report paths\n\nFrontend (React):\n- fix async result race: gate cancellation on real unmount, not the computing-flip teardown\n- remove console.debug; log swallowed errors\n- cancel affordance + client poll timeout; block blank-path full-repo traversal\n- distinct, actionable error/success messages\n- harden snapshot import (size/depth/node caps, finite numbers, prototype-pollution keys)\n- DRY JContentLink component\n- AAA: focus-visible, 44px targets, contrast >=7:1, progress live region + aria-valuetext, reduced-motion tick\n- jest --coverage + lcov; new extractTree/toFlameNode/table tests\n\nTests: jsEscape, JcrStatsService gate/elapsed, data-carrier getters.\nDocs: document the async API + progress/resume; correct the system-session ACL claim; add Known Limitations.\n\nQuality gate OK (0 open issues, coverage 0->39%); 28/28 Cypress E2E green; 52 Java + 84 JS unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review findings (no-result feedback, unmount guard, traversal cap off-by-one)\n\n- JcrStats.jsx: surface an error message when the server finishes with no result\n  (was a silent blank UI); guard the polling effect against unmount; restore an\n  explicit null guard in readFile before the onTree callback.\n- jcrStatsUtils.js: validateNode depth check uses >= so the enforced limit matches\n  MAX_IMPORT_DEPTH exactly.\n- JcrStatsComputer.java: MAX_VISITED_NODES check uses >= to honor the stated cap.\n- JcrStatsService.java: drop the dead null check in deactivate() (executor is final).\n\n28/28 Cypress E2E green; 52 Java + 84 JS unit tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): link text contrast to AAA 7:1 (#006fa0 -> #005a82)\n\nFinal-pass WCAG 2.2 AAA review: the \"Open in jContent\" link text used #006fa0\n(~5.9:1 on white — AA only). Darkened to #005a82 (~7.1:1) to meet SC 1.4.6.\nThe description left-border keeps #006fa0 (non-text UI boundary, SC 1.4.11 needs only 3:1);\ncomments corrected to reflect the right thresholds.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXLLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACFMQAGKzh6vDWjIj8GN4RnuevSL+\nUid4FvuIWcnTu+7zcL6Km1NiaQCA7UGY75iCKE23nW8z+hBPkp4IIXDmKELS/BWR\nbYHQ8jI13THiYPJhdYS3/JOa9ndoa2wgC2ALYac0T5+4qpYhRGeaFKjYexSb48WD\n1/WwARcKhkCcjORcWZLE2L7eMr2I+Bb0jdqTf6N+6qHW0bKqi8Vjv6Wve6R632og\nR3IhUii6P1ZcakLmreYN7b0sDDGhFTUu9g2feTDoRAaasZL9LUDc/Dmy38LUACX8\ngQFVg1+xfs451PlaUKzRE2apJQRKP+Sz7ywhNXV0SJhG/Z7WzcYEH89TSWo5+baL\nOfFgoqO7GNSw/cqUzTn7sc89MdUSoTKjCOrx0Q0/yPaRr7h236D1pxp5MtIm9P1m\nG9RVpGmZqIredsmXDDuDCrH/S5RLdK6L6Zrj41xZ3ZbblmLL9tpb+aG1TEfbSRrB\neda1dQZLgS7Jf6sqZ3XTOmKL/eCLa/0OfDtXmK3/MVtd/KccsYU1fCkTCDyFxb6K\neVcfy4yzsKMRcmoP+PfpJ3lnLJcTDAl8qsbzubCkWwDRD+5q0M46wZSAylEvTDkj\nGQymnCHGRuLmDnUPA2z3wOQYMsrxwm8sgqd/h1xWkLEoAIV8Jdj0ZE2yqDamLI5C\nTaARHR3VVQlwFLWmhNAy\n=drHW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:37:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKDU1MzlhYTEwZTM3Y2VkOTIxODMwNzZlODE5ZjdiZTgxMWY3NjQxMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d","sha":"4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d"}],"sha":"5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/5539aa10e37ced92183076e819f7be811f76410d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T14:55:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T14:55:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: asynchronous JCR computation (compute/status/result) to avoid request timeouts (#5)\n\n* feat: asynchronous JCR computation to avoid request timeouts\n\nA full subtree traversal (e.g. /sites) can take long enough to time out a\nsynchronous GraphQL request. Run it in the background instead:\n- JcrStatsService (OSGi @Component): single-thread executor runs the traversal\n  off-request and caches the result + running/error state (one at a time).\n- GraphQL: jcrStats.compute(path) mutation starts the job (no-op if already\n  running); jcrStats.status query reports running/path/error/hasResult;\n  jcrStats.result(maxDepth) returns the cached tree. (Sync tree/size/nodeCount\n  kept for direct API use.)\n- Admin UI: Compute now starts the job and polls status every 2s, then fetches\n  result — no long-held request. Load/Save/Compare unchanged.\n- Tests: async API test (compute -> status -> result). mvn 24, jest 48,\n  eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 28/28.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: progress bar, elapsed timer and running-job status resume\n\nSurface live computation progress in the admin UI and keep it visible when\nnavigating away and back:\n\n- Poll the async job status (elapsedMs + visitedCount) and render a progress\n  bar, a smoothly-ticking elapsed timer and a scanned-node counter while a\n  computation runs.\n- On (re)mount, resume the live status of a still-running job. A finished\n  result is intentionally NOT auto-restored: that would asynchronously clobber\n  a tree the user has since loaded from a file and surface another user''s run.\n- JcrStatsService exposes startedAt/elapsedMs/visitedCount; the computer\n  increments a shared visited counter as it walks the tree.\n- E2E: gate each admin test on the shared async job being idle so a long job\n  from a previous test is not picked up by the next (resume-on-mount).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb22d80ad5550bfbba4b98623ee976c0fbd6b27a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/cb22d80ad5550bfbba4b98623ee976c0fbd6b27a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d","verification":{"payload":"tree cb22d80ad5550bfbba4b98623ee976c0fbd6b27a\nparent bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782140145 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782140145 +0200\n\nfeat: asynchronous JCR computation (compute/status/result) to avoid request timeouts (#5)\n\n* feat: asynchronous JCR computation to avoid request timeouts\n\nA full subtree traversal (e.g. /sites) can take long enough to time out a\nsynchronous GraphQL request. Run it in the background instead:\n- JcrStatsService (OSGi @Component): single-thread executor runs the traversal\n  off-request and caches the result + running/error state (one at a time).\n- GraphQL: jcrStats.compute(path) mutation starts the job (no-op if already\n  running); jcrStats.status query reports running/path/error/hasResult;\n  jcrStats.result(maxDepth) returns the cached tree. (Sync tree/size/nodeCount\n  kept for direct API use.)\n- Admin UI: Compute now starts the job and polls status every 2s, then fetches\n  result — no long-held request. Load/Save/Compare unchanged.\n- Tests: async API test (compute -> status -> result). mvn 24, jest 48,\n  eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 28/28.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: progress bar, elapsed timer and running-job status resume\n\nSurface live computation progress in the admin UI and keep it visible when\nnavigating away and back:\n\n- Poll the async job status (elapsedMs + visitedCount) and render a progress\n  bar, a smoothly-ticking elapsed timer and a scanned-node counter while a\n  computation runs.\n- On (re)mount, resume the live status of a still-running job. A finished\n  result is intentionally NOT auto-restored: that would asynchronously clobber\n  a tree the user has since loaded from a file and surface another user''s run.\n- JcrStatsService exposes startedAt/elapsedMs/visitedCount; the computer\n  increments a shared visited counter as it walks the tree.\n- E2E: gate each admin test on the shared async job being idle so a long job\n  from a previous test is not picked up by the next (resume-on-mount).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOUzxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMT0QADpSel0XE5053dM9vH9DbPnx\nhOk9OU/sVEebC93K4QAgAtXwW+oCiQGH+6TC431yRbBK6n+B2B4TQtpqRzu+FYpI\nky1WlL733orbHNhVr/PKpEb9uYT5+1q44CUADmpOxeHdSqKvm5Fd1ZIWI+nn9875\n6NzjMyy6vOA8PpEWc5ej+3eD0ywmkngWj9/rBv1NIV6nNu1UkE9TA9/2O+UC0zRO\nLlPV5XVlsMB6NJz3Nt245HGsTIWn8aG035VGjGUz7q+Ume41ZHnG3iRagliZPzlm\n5tidJdoZE0IuMk1//lKeW32ezOoOU7vzAwx8vAFYDNY2F+ZsrO8BK5yy6o1XuM/S\nWKsTeQbDyvYdxCEXpUXmuLL5mUT58sNrtHMTFrCW3w81KCG9vFCKPhyvbErSHt/N\nj0kriNODVP51MqG6cPYLS6FJ8dVEn7w3jZLsyurSW5kV8COtEuGqEr1X7pM3zKx+\n9n70BmhK+nXhkQ2qFze8lOkg44CqkrO0R1ZGJIrnH+ZfJ3ittLAoy4ftJgG4Vity\nx4z+cgfO+/ppMGjMgvnuIJTiRVgHwJpGUzs12c3wlEDQAkqJzz5y8yMyvxY9MUlA\n7a8Gp4fJ3lmvead6viPzx8XtrQu3tXhakcpHmPs2RZB5o+0jcdr3dfjHFaxeJu/p\nZaxeTRdUibMpgQ5Q95y8\n=+rBa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T14:55:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKDRlM2VkMTQyYjhmNWFlMWI0NmRiZjBjZmE5MGJkMjY4NmQzY2Q2NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7","sha":"bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7"}],"sha":"4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/4e3ed142b8f5ae1b46dbf0cfa90bd2686d3cd64d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T10:08:12Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T10:08:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: JCR Stats analyzer — GraphQL API + interactive admin UI (flamegraph/table/diff, jContent) (#4)\n\n* feat: add jcrStats GraphQL API + admin UI and Cypress E2E tests\n\nMake the JCR size computation reachable over HTTP so it can be exercised by\nthe standard @jahia/cypress Docker harness (the Karaf command alone is not\ntestable from Cypress).\n\n- Extract the compute + flamegraph logic from ComputeSizeCommand into a\n  reusable JcrStatsComputer (command now delegates); add ComputeResult and a\n  node-count helper. Unit tests migrated to JcrStatsComputerTest.\n- GraphQL: single ''jcrStats'' namespace on Query/Mutation\n  (query size/nodeCount/reports, mutation computeSize), each gated by\n  @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"jcrStatsAdmin\").\n- Admin UI: React micro-frontend at /jahia/administration/jcrStatsExecution\n  (moonstone + ui-extender + module-federation), built via frontend-maven-plugin.\n- RBAC: ship jcrStatsAdmin permission + jcr-stats-administrator role (import.zip).\n- pom: graphql-dxm-provider + graphql deps, frontend build, export-package;\n  bump to 2.1.0-SNAPSHOT.\n- tests/: @jahia/cypress Docker harness with 3 specs (GraphQL API, admin UI,\n  fine-grained permission enforcement). Full Docker E2E: 14/14 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: visualize the generated flamegraph directly from the admin UI\n\n- Expose flamegraphUrl on jcrStats.computeSize and url on jcrStats.reports\n  (Jahia file-servlet URL: /files/default<path>), via a shared\n  JcrStatsComputer.flamegraphUrl helper.\n- Admin UI embeds the generated flamegraph in an iframe and offers an\n  ''open in new tab'' link; report rows are now clickable links to each flamegraph.\n- Tests: assert the new url fields (API spec) and that the embedded iframe''s\n  source serves the renderable flamegraph HTML in an authenticated session\n  (admin UI spec). Full Docker E2E: 15/15 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render an interactive flamegraph in-app with react-flame-graph\n\nAdd a client-side flamegraph alongside the server-generated HTML report:\n- GraphQL: new recursive JcrStatsNode type + jcrStats.tree(path, maxDepth)\n  exposing the size-weighted node tree (sizes fully aggregated, children\n  pruned below maxDepth to bound the payload).\n- Admin UI: render react-flame-graph from jcrStats.tree directly in React\n  (no iframe, no file-servlet dependency); the server HTML report stays as\n  the durable / Karaf-command artifact below it.\n- Tests: assert the tree contract + maxDepth pruning (API spec) and that the\n  React flamegraph renders in-app (admin UI spec). Full Docker E2E: 18/18.\n\nNote: react-flame-graph 1.4.0 declares a React 15/16 peer range; it renders\ncorrectly under the module''s React 18 (verified by E2E) — peer warning only.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: flamegraph-only responsive admin UI\n\n- Remove the generated HTML report (iframe + open-in-new-tab + reports list)\n  from the admin UI; the interactive react-flame-graph is now the sole view.\n  The ''Compute size'' action loads jcrStats.tree only (no HTML file written\n  from the UI). The Karaf command + computeSize/reports GraphQL still generate\n  the HTML artifact for CLI/API consumers.\n- Make the flamegraph responsive: full-width container, width measured from the\n  container and height from the window, both updated on resize.\n- Fix React error #185 (infinite update loop): memoize the flame data so its\n  identity is stable and guard setDimensions to bail when unchanged.\n- Tests updated: assert flamegraph-only UI (no iframe/reports) + responsive\n  width. Full Docker E2E: 16/16.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): fit the flamegraph height within the viewport\n\nMeasure the flamegraph container''s actual top offset (getBoundingClientRect)\nand size its height to window.innerHeight - top - margin, instead of\nsubtracting a fixed offset from the window height. The fixed offset\nunder-counted the chrome above the graph (admin top bar + header + form),\nso the flamegraph extended past the bottom of the window. Adds an E2E\nassertion that the flamegraph bottom stays within the viewport. E2E: 16/16.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): flamegraph click feedback + Ctrl+Enter submit\n\n- Wire react-flame-graph onChange to report the focused frame in the caption,\n  so clicking a frame is visibly acknowledged (it also zooms natively). The\n  click target is the SVG <rect>; the label <div> is pointer-events:none.\n- Ctrl+Enter (and Cmd+Enter) in the path field submits the form.\n- E2E: click-by-coordinate focus test + Ctrl+Enter submit test. 18/18 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): selectable size/node-count metric + click perf & error fixes\n\n- Weight the flamegraph by aggregated size OR aggregated node count, chosen via\n  a selector. Backend: JcrStatsNode exposes nodeCount (countNodes made static);\n  GET_TREE fetches it; the React value/caption switch on the chosen metric.\n- Focus caption shows the real measure: read it from react-flame-graph''s\n  node.source (the chart node carries width, not the original value).\n- Surface query failures: handleCompute checks for actual tree data instead of\n  assuming success, so a failed jcrStats.tree shows an error instead of a blank\n  panel (no silent failure).\n- Click performance: disable react-flame-graph''s 200ms SVG transition (animating\n  every rect/g on focus janked clicks even on small instances); zoom is now instant.\n- Tests: tree.nodeCount (API), node-count metric toggle (UI). Full E2E: 19/19.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): save/load flamegraph data for offline analysis\n\n- Save data: export the current jcrStats.tree to a JSON file\n  ({format, version, path, maxDepth, exportedAt, tree}) via a client-side\n  download — no server round-trip.\n- Load data: import a saved file and render the flamegraph from it without\n  recomputing; accepts the export envelope or a raw tree node, with defensive\n  validation/coercion since the file content is untrusted.\n- Tree is now component state, fed by either the GraphQL query or an import.\n- Tests: import-from-file renders the loaded tree; Save button appears once a\n  graph is shown (fixture cypress/fixtures/sample-flamegraph.json). E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): add icons to the action buttons\n\nUse moonstone icons on the flamegraph actions: Compute size (Bar/chart),\nLoad data (Upload/import), Save data (Download/export). Labels are kept, so\nbehaviour and selectors are unchanged. Full E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(ui): default the path to /sites instead of /sites/systemsite\n\nScans all sites by default. Updated the default-value assertion and the\ndefault-path tests (root is now ''sites''); explicit /sites/systemsite tests\nunchanged. E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: tree-table + %/Top-N, snapshot diff, and open-in-jContent\n\nAnalyzer features atop the flamegraph:\n- View switcher: Flamegraph / Tree table / Largest items. Table shows size,\n  % of total, % of parent and node count (expandable); Largest is a Top-N by\n  the active metric. New TreeTable/TopList components + jcrStatsUtils helpers.\n- Snapshot diff: ''Compare with…'' loads a baseline file and shows a per-path\n  delta table (baseline vs current, sorted by |Δ|). New DiffTable component.\n- Open in jContent: each node deep-links into jContent (buildJContentUrl);\n  also on the focused flamegraph node. Backend: JcrStatsNode exposes ''path''.\n- Tests: tree-table %, largest + jContent links, snapshot diff. E2E: 24/24.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve 7 code-review findings in JcrStatsComputer and NodeStats\n\n1. CRITICAL (S5131): add jsEscape() to sanitize node names embedded in\n   JS f(...) calls — escapes \\, \", <, >, /, CR, LF, U+2028, U+2029.\n\n2. HIGH (O(n²) nodeCount): accumulate nodeCount in NodeStats.addSubNodeStats()\n   (init=1, += child.getNodeCount()); countNodes() now delegates to\n   getNodeCount() — O(1) instead of full subtree recursion per node.\n\n3. HIGH (NPE risk): change NodeStats.size from boxed Long to primitive long; update setSize/getSize/addSize signatures accordingly.\n\n4. HIGH (silent corrupt upload): writeGraphData() tracks dataWritten flag —\n   returns null without uploading when writeGraphNode throws; also adds\n   null-checks + IllegalStateException for missing template resources in\n   writeGraphHeader/Footer.\n\n5. MEDIUM: replace SimpleDateFormat + new Date() with static final\n   DateTimeFormatter + LocalDateTime.now().\n\n6. MEDIUM: remove per-node bufferedWriter.flush() inside writeGraphNode\n   recursion (try-with-resources close() flushes once).\n\n7. MEDIUM: name the magic 0 in f(...) as FLAMEGRAPH_STACK_DEPTH constant.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add flamegraphUrl, nodeCount, GqlNodeStats depth, JS utils and Cypress tests\n\nJava (JcrStatsComputerTest):\n- flamegraphUrl(null) == null; flamegraphUrl(path) prepends /files/default prefix\n- nodeCount accumulation: 4-node tree (root+childA+grandChild+childB) asserts\n  getNodeCount()==4 and countNodes(root)==4\n- GqlNodeStats depth-0: children empty but nodeCount reflects full subtree\n- GqlNodeStats depth-1: immediate children exposed, grandchildren pruned,\n  nodeCount still covers the whole subtree\n\nJS (jcrStatsUtils.test.js, new Jest harness):\n- 46 unit tests covering all exported pure functions with edge cases:\n  formatBytes (0, negative, NaN, null, undefined, Infinity, -0, KB/MB/GB rollover),\n  measureOf (size/nodes metrics, non-finite inputs),\n  percent (whole=0 guard, normal values, overflow),\n  flatten (root exclusion, depth tracking, coercions, missing children),\n  buildJContentUrl (non-/sites paths, null inputs, segment encoding, language param,\n  traversal stripping),\n  diffTrees (positive/negative delta, sort order, empty-string path falls back to name),\n  signedBytes (zero, positive +, negative -)\n- Jest added as standalone devDep (not wired into Maven/webpack build)\n\nCypress:\n- 02-jcrStatsAdmin: malformed JSON file load shows [role=alert] and no flamegraph\n- 03-jcrStats-Permissions: denied user calling computeSize mutation gets\n  \"Permission denied\" error; mirrors existing getSize denial pattern\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve code-review findings (a11y AAA, ergonomy, JS quality, docs)\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): accessible names on glyph/icon controls and\njContent links, scope on table headers, labelled file inputs, focus moved to\nresults on view change, landmarks, AAA-contrast text/focus colours, single\nrole=alert, reduced-motion block, keyboard-access note for the flamegraph.\nErgonomy: neutral ''Compute'' label, empty-state + baseline-loaded guidance,\nLoad/Compare disabled while computing, tables remount on new data.\nJS quality: encode jContent URL segments, drop bootstrap console.log, eslint\nconfig added + 0 lint errors. Docs: README rewritten (UI, GraphQL API,\npermission, build, tests). All verified: mvn 24 unit tests, jest 46, lint 0,\nfull Cypress E2E 26/26.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR-review findings\n\n- HIGH: contain IllegalStateException from a missing flamegraph template in\n  writeGraphFile (log + return null) instead of letting it escape the public API.\n- MED: jsEscape emits \\u000D/\\u000A for CR/LF (matches the Unicode-escape policy).\n- MED: buildJContentUrl now encodes the site segment too.\n- LOW: README button label ''Compute size'' -> ''Compute''; add a positive\n  computeSize-allowed permission test.\nVerified: mvn 24 unit tests, jest 46, eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 27/27.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): open nodes in the correct jContent section (media/pages/content-folders)\n\nbuildJContentUrl hardcoded the content-folders section. Choose it from the\nsite-relative root: files -> media, contents -> content-folders, else (page\ntree) -> pages. e.g. /sites/digitall/files/images/slides now links to\n/jahia/jcontent/digitall/en/media/files/images/slides. Updated jest tests\n(+2 media/pages cases) and hardened slow-admin-shell initial-render assertions\nwith a 30s timeout. Jest 48, eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 27/27.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"16023599e0ef47328287b44ad016c83a381fe603","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/16023599e0ef47328287b44ad016c83a381fe603"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 16023599e0ef47328287b44ad016c83a381fe603\nparent 52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1782122892 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782122892 +0200\n\nfeat: JCR Stats analyzer — GraphQL API + interactive admin UI (flamegraph/table/diff, jContent) (#4)\n\n* feat: add jcrStats GraphQL API + admin UI and Cypress E2E tests\n\nMake the JCR size computation reachable over HTTP so it can be exercised by\nthe standard @jahia/cypress Docker harness (the Karaf command alone is not\ntestable from Cypress).\n\n- Extract the compute + flamegraph logic from ComputeSizeCommand into a\n  reusable JcrStatsComputer (command now delegates); add ComputeResult and a\n  node-count helper. Unit tests migrated to JcrStatsComputerTest.\n- GraphQL: single ''jcrStats'' namespace on Query/Mutation\n  (query size/nodeCount/reports, mutation computeSize), each gated by\n  @GraphQLRequiresPermission(\"jcrStatsAdmin\").\n- Admin UI: React micro-frontend at /jahia/administration/jcrStatsExecution\n  (moonstone + ui-extender + module-federation), built via frontend-maven-plugin.\n- RBAC: ship jcrStatsAdmin permission + jcr-stats-administrator role (import.zip).\n- pom: graphql-dxm-provider + graphql deps, frontend build, export-package;\n  bump to 2.1.0-SNAPSHOT.\n- tests/: @jahia/cypress Docker harness with 3 specs (GraphQL API, admin UI,\n  fine-grained permission enforcement). Full Docker E2E: 14/14 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: visualize the generated flamegraph directly from the admin UI\n\n- Expose flamegraphUrl on jcrStats.computeSize and url on jcrStats.reports\n  (Jahia file-servlet URL: /files/default<path>), via a shared\n  JcrStatsComputer.flamegraphUrl helper.\n- Admin UI embeds the generated flamegraph in an iframe and offers an\n  ''open in new tab'' link; report rows are now clickable links to each flamegraph.\n- Tests: assert the new url fields (API spec) and that the embedded iframe''s\n  source serves the renderable flamegraph HTML in an authenticated session\n  (admin UI spec). Full Docker E2E: 15/15 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: render an interactive flamegraph in-app with react-flame-graph\n\nAdd a client-side flamegraph alongside the server-generated HTML report:\n- GraphQL: new recursive JcrStatsNode type + jcrStats.tree(path, maxDepth)\n  exposing the size-weighted node tree (sizes fully aggregated, children\n  pruned below maxDepth to bound the payload).\n- Admin UI: render react-flame-graph from jcrStats.tree directly in React\n  (no iframe, no file-servlet dependency); the server HTML report stays as\n  the durable / Karaf-command artifact below it.\n- Tests: assert the tree contract + maxDepth pruning (API spec) and that the\n  React flamegraph renders in-app (admin UI spec). Full Docker E2E: 18/18.\n\nNote: react-flame-graph 1.4.0 declares a React 15/16 peer range; it renders\ncorrectly under the module''s React 18 (verified by E2E) — peer warning only.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: flamegraph-only responsive admin UI\n\n- Remove the generated HTML report (iframe + open-in-new-tab + reports list)\n  from the admin UI; the interactive react-flame-graph is now the sole view.\n  The ''Compute size'' action loads jcrStats.tree only (no HTML file written\n  from the UI). The Karaf command + computeSize/reports GraphQL still generate\n  the HTML artifact for CLI/API consumers.\n- Make the flamegraph responsive: full-width container, width measured from the\n  container and height from the window, both updated on resize.\n- Fix React error #185 (infinite update loop): memoize the flame data so its\n  identity is stable and guard setDimensions to bail when unchanged.\n- Tests updated: assert flamegraph-only UI (no iframe/reports) + responsive\n  width. Full Docker E2E: 16/16.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): fit the flamegraph height within the viewport\n\nMeasure the flamegraph container''s actual top offset (getBoundingClientRect)\nand size its height to window.innerHeight - top - margin, instead of\nsubtracting a fixed offset from the window height. The fixed offset\nunder-counted the chrome above the graph (admin top bar + header + form),\nso the flamegraph extended past the bottom of the window. Adds an E2E\nassertion that the flamegraph bottom stays within the viewport. E2E: 16/16.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): flamegraph click feedback + Ctrl+Enter submit\n\n- Wire react-flame-graph onChange to report the focused frame in the caption,\n  so clicking a frame is visibly acknowledged (it also zooms natively). The\n  click target is the SVG <rect>; the label <div> is pointer-events:none.\n- Ctrl+Enter (and Cmd+Enter) in the path field submits the form.\n- E2E: click-by-coordinate focus test + Ctrl+Enter submit test. 18/18 passing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): selectable size/node-count metric + click perf & error fixes\n\n- Weight the flamegraph by aggregated size OR aggregated node count, chosen via\n  a selector. Backend: JcrStatsNode exposes nodeCount (countNodes made static);\n  GET_TREE fetches it; the React value/caption switch on the chosen metric.\n- Focus caption shows the real measure: read it from react-flame-graph''s\n  node.source (the chart node carries width, not the original value).\n- Surface query failures: handleCompute checks for actual tree data instead of\n  assuming success, so a failed jcrStats.tree shows an error instead of a blank\n  panel (no silent failure).\n- Click performance: disable react-flame-graph''s 200ms SVG transition (animating\n  every rect/g on focus janked clicks even on small instances); zoom is now instant.\n- Tests: tree.nodeCount (API), node-count metric toggle (UI). Full E2E: 19/19.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): save/load flamegraph data for offline analysis\n\n- Save data: export the current jcrStats.tree to a JSON file\n  ({format, version, path, maxDepth, exportedAt, tree}) via a client-side\n  download — no server round-trip.\n- Load data: import a saved file and render the flamegraph from it without\n  recomputing; accepts the export envelope or a raw tree node, with defensive\n  validation/coercion since the file content is untrusted.\n- Tree is now component state, fed by either the GraphQL query or an import.\n- Tests: import-from-file renders the loaded tree; Save button appears once a\n  graph is shown (fixture cypress/fixtures/sample-flamegraph.json). E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat(ui): add icons to the action buttons\n\nUse moonstone icons on the flamegraph actions: Compute size (Bar/chart),\nLoad data (Upload/import), Save data (Download/export). Labels are kept, so\nbehaviour and selectors are unchanged. Full E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* chore(ui): default the path to /sites instead of /sites/systemsite\n\nScans all sites by default. Updated the default-value assertion and the\ndefault-path tests (root is now ''sites''); explicit /sites/systemsite tests\nunchanged. E2E: 21/21.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: tree-table + %/Top-N, snapshot diff, and open-in-jContent\n\nAnalyzer features atop the flamegraph:\n- View switcher: Flamegraph / Tree table / Largest items. Table shows size,\n  % of total, % of parent and node count (expandable); Largest is a Top-N by\n  the active metric. New TreeTable/TopList components + jcrStatsUtils helpers.\n- Snapshot diff: ''Compare with…'' loads a baseline file and shows a per-path\n  delta table (baseline vs current, sorted by |Δ|). New DiffTable component.\n- Open in jContent: each node deep-links into jContent (buildJContentUrl);\n  also on the focused flamegraph node. Backend: JcrStatsNode exposes ''path''.\n- Tests: tree-table %, largest + jContent links, snapshot diff. E2E: 24/24.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve 7 code-review findings in JcrStatsComputer and NodeStats\n\n1. CRITICAL (S5131): add jsEscape() to sanitize node names embedded in\n   JS f(...) calls — escapes \\, \", <, >, /, CR, LF, U+2028, U+2029.\n\n2. HIGH (O(n²) nodeCount): accumulate nodeCount in NodeStats.addSubNodeStats()\n   (init=1, += child.getNodeCount()); countNodes() now delegates to\n   getNodeCount() — O(1) instead of full subtree recursion per node.\n\n3. HIGH (NPE risk): change NodeStats.size from boxed Long to primitive long; update setSize/getSize/addSize signatures accordingly.\n\n4. HIGH (silent corrupt upload): writeGraphData() tracks dataWritten flag —\n   returns null without uploading when writeGraphNode throws; also adds\n   null-checks + IllegalStateException for missing template resources in\n   writeGraphHeader/Footer.\n\n5. MEDIUM: replace SimpleDateFormat + new Date() with static final\n   DateTimeFormatter + LocalDateTime.now().\n\n6. MEDIUM: remove per-node bufferedWriter.flush() inside writeGraphNode\n   recursion (try-with-resources close() flushes once).\n\n7. MEDIUM: name the magic 0 in f(...) as FLAMEGRAPH_STACK_DEPTH constant.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add flamegraphUrl, nodeCount, GqlNodeStats depth, JS utils and Cypress tests\n\nJava (JcrStatsComputerTest):\n- flamegraphUrl(null) == null; flamegraphUrl(path) prepends /files/default prefix\n- nodeCount accumulation: 4-node tree (root+childA+grandChild+childB) asserts\n  getNodeCount()==4 and countNodes(root)==4\n- GqlNodeStats depth-0: children empty but nodeCount reflects full subtree\n- GqlNodeStats depth-1: immediate children exposed, grandchildren pruned,\n  nodeCount still covers the whole subtree\n\nJS (jcrStatsUtils.test.js, new Jest harness):\n- 46 unit tests covering all exported pure functions with edge cases:\n  formatBytes (0, negative, NaN, null, undefined, Infinity, -0, KB/MB/GB rollover),\n  measureOf (size/nodes metrics, non-finite inputs),\n  percent (whole=0 guard, normal values, overflow),\n  flatten (root exclusion, depth tracking, coercions, missing children),\n  buildJContentUrl (non-/sites paths, null inputs, segment encoding, language param,\n  traversal stripping),\n  diffTrees (positive/negative delta, sort order, empty-string path falls back to name),\n  signedBytes (zero, positive +, negative -)\n- Jest added as standalone devDep (not wired into Maven/webpack build)\n\nCypress:\n- 02-jcrStatsAdmin: malformed JSON file load shows [role=alert] and no flamegraph\n- 03-jcrStats-Permissions: denied user calling computeSize mutation gets\n  \"Permission denied\" error; mirrors existing getSize denial pattern\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve code-review findings (a11y AAA, ergonomy, JS quality, docs)\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA): accessible names on glyph/icon controls and\njContent links, scope on table headers, labelled file inputs, focus moved to\nresults on view change, landmarks, AAA-contrast text/focus colours, single\nrole=alert, reduced-motion block, keyboard-access note for the flamegraph.\nErgonomy: neutral ''Compute'' label, empty-state + baseline-loaded guidance,\nLoad/Compare disabled while computing, tables remount on new data.\nJS quality: encode jContent URL segments, drop bootstrap console.log, eslint\nconfig added + 0 lint errors. Docs: README rewritten (UI, GraphQL API,\npermission, build, tests). All verified: mvn 24 unit tests, jest 46, lint 0,\nfull Cypress E2E 26/26.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address blind PR-review findings\n\n- HIGH: contain IllegalStateException from a missing flamegraph template in\n  writeGraphFile (log + return null) instead of letting it escape the public API.\n- MED: jsEscape emits \\u000D/\\u000A for CR/LF (matches the Unicode-escape policy).\n- MED: buildJContentUrl now encodes the site segment too.\n- LOW: README button label ''Compute size'' -> ''Compute''; add a positive\n  computeSize-allowed permission test.\nVerified: mvn 24 unit tests, jest 46, eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 27/27.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(ui): open nodes in the correct jContent section (media/pages/content-folders)\n\nbuildJContentUrl hardcoded the content-folders section. Choose it from the\nsite-relative root: files -> media, contents -> content-folders, else (page\ntree) -> pages. e.g. /sites/digitall/files/images/slides now links to\n/jahia/jcontent/digitall/en/media/files/images/slides. Updated jest tests\n(+2 media/pages cases) and hardened slow-admin-shell initial-render assertions\nwith a 30s timeout. Jest 48, eslint 0, full Cypress E2E 27/27.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOQmMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAboAQAJgrutzrhBA8BN3VCvZsufLO\n+diS7i8e9kAsBnuUW1qUTS7dtivvuXkrN6V1svHvtv8BTbv6QJEG6BLbnHn25BWx\nvlRBLyROVaqRPVXBSGvYDvt9/6gxnRPtMR+2PhSuu/pmyxtPRsBch5g6sU85SoAW\nCY1Qve1MDUh6YaQdmh5+h9byt8S5SXacsFEiCeskpyieyROaXtt1Uj9ExbKzSF3/\nUOMQ6gUnn2uUYx9OGqWdR7Apt2fhvtMNkpx6HRbEPBUIAs8TSWSCWvugBInalY0m\nFEwCmOWDfT73OYtsaLeM/XDGXdhJjGb7UTEkKliIBSbuxuyDkpFaTxHMtsZE4Nwo\n5dKKvAGjQ4YTOpTCvpOu4zAkH9uSWFcfHzWHl6itIqg0/JIyc3mcw2o/9seh8RNJ\nswVx4VsVZoTcGALljv2tf+ikrx0Fq8MTiTYlXE1prcLpTvsTJsopul7YcFWSnOt6\neOL6/aJo4lL0BDSXmIt4qPcSItVv+F+tM1hZzOfGiitj7QAo8fK7rGjoIapxK85r\nomjOSK0V543RjWXwqqT4EHTLoI7uymR5ifGxEqD7k4jh2IDmbW0PL0keCgOSR2bj\na6vNQX6rvybSyJCsfz0FoeYuxHJXiipyIpNyuaWrq3RU/W1BYPqHO4cPrrCEqeqw\nyn5Y36euB32KZJyYE+Sw\n=uiSV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T10:08:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7","node_id":"C_kwDOGd35idoAKGJmODcyODAyMDhiMDQ1ZWFkYTNmYzExYmU2OGVhNGNiZDc2NjE4Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-stats/commit/52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8","sha":"52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8"}],"sha":"bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/bf87280208b045eada3fc11be68ea4cbd76618f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/commits/52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:00Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden jcr-stats: fix NodeStats sibling data loss, clean up compute-size, add tests (#3)\n\n* fix: correct sibling data loss in NodeStats; harden compute-size command + add tests\n\n- NodeStats.compareTo was ordered by size only while equals/hashCode use\n  path+size+children. As subNodeStats is a TreeSet (which uses compareTo for\n  uniqueness), two siblings of equal size collapsed to one and the second was\n  silently dropped — yet its size was still added, so the tree and totals\n  disagreed and the flamegraph lost nodes. compareTo is now a total order:\n  size descending, tie-broken by the (unique) node path.\n- ComputeSizeCommand: expand wildcard imports, reduce method visibility to\n  private (only execute() is the entry point), rename the recursive\n  writeGraphData overload to writeGraphNode, remove a dead unused FileWriter in\n  the upload block, use parameterized logging, and null-guard temp-file cleanup.\n- pom.xml: remove commented-out require-capability line (Sonar xml:S125).\n- Add JUnit4 + AssertJ tests (15) for NodeStats (incl. the equal-size sibling\n  regression) and the flamegraph writer.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: apply PR-review fixes for correctness, charset safety, and test quality\n\nH1 (blocker): make equals/hashCode use path-only identity in NodeStats.\n  Two nodes with the same JCR path are the same node regardless of size or\n  children; this keeps equals consistent with compareTo''s path tie-break and\n  prevents a TreeSet contract violation (compareTo==0 but equals==false).\n\nH2: replace FileWriter with OutputStreamWriter+UTF_8 at both call sites in\n  ComputeSizeCommand (writeGraphData and writeGraphFooter) so non-ASCII node\n  names on localised sites are never corrupted by the JVM default charset.\n\nM4: change writeGraphNode startPosition parameter from Long to primitive long\n  to eliminate boxing and any NPE risk in the recursive size accumulation.\n\nL1: remove the redundant isDebugEnabled guard around the parameterised\n  LOGGER.debug call; SLF4J evaluates arguments lazily so the guard is noise.\n\nM1: add compareTo_reflexive test to NodeStatsTest.\nM2: tighten startPositionAdvancesAcrossSiblings assertions to full\n  f(level,start,size,0,\"name\") line matches so a wrong-level regression is caught.\nM3: invokeWriteGraphNode helper now declares throws Exception and no longer\n  wraps RepositoryException inside IOException, preserving the original type.\n\nTest: update equals_differentSize_areNotEqual → equals_samePathDifferentSize_areEqual\n  to reflect path-only identity (same path = equal regardless of size).\n\nAll 16 tests pass (NodeStatsTest: 12, ComputeSizeCommandTest: 4).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: address PR review (equals/compareTo consistency, UTF-8 output)\n\n- NodeStats equals/hashCode now key on path only (a node''s identity is its\n  unique JCR path; size and children are derived), making them consistent with\n  compareTo''s tie-break so the TreeSet never collapses distinct nodes\n- ComputeSizeCommand: write the flamegraph via UTF-8 OutputStreamWriter instead\n  of platform-default FileWriter (fixes mojibake for non-ASCII node names);\n  use primitive long for the recursive startPosition; keep the isDebugEnabled\n  guard since the debug arg (byteCountToDisplaySize) is evaluated eagerly\n- Tests: add compareTo reflexivity, full-line assertions for the sibling\n  start-position case, helper no longer erases RepositoryException type\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: manage FileOutputStream as a try-with-resources variable\n\nDeclare the FileOutputStream as its own TWR resource at both flamegraph writer\nsites instead of constructing it inline inside OutputStreamWriter, so it is\nalways closed even if the writer constructor fails (Sonar S2095).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"44ea190ab3ea8615afb94dc736f35e1ec3790b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/trees/44ea190ab3ea8615afb94dc736f35e1ec3790b89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-stats/git/commits/52439dffe9548c87fbdf14ce39460e7a5fc596c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 44ea190ab3ea8615afb94dc736f35e1ec3790b89\nparent eb6cfc4fa103d794f9dacce98c1be7d43feabf4c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781976660 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781976660 +0200\n\nHarden jcr-stats: fix NodeStats sibling data loss, clean up compute-size, add tests (#3)\n\n* fix: correct sibling data loss in NodeStats; harden compute-size command + add tests\n\n- NodeStats.compareTo was ordered by size only while equals/hashCode use\n  path+size+children. As subNodeStats is a TreeSet (which uses compareTo for\n  uniqueness), two siblings of equal size collapsed to one and the second was\n  silently dropped — yet its size was still added, so the tree and totals\n  disagreed and the flamegraph lost nodes. compareTo is now a total order:\n  size descending, tie-broken by the (unique) node path.\n- ComputeSizeCommand: expand wildcard imports, reduce method visibility to\n  private (only execute() is the entry point), rename the recursive\n  writeGraphData overload to writeGraphNode, remove a dead unused FileWriter in\n  the upload block, use parameterized logging, and null-guard temp-file cleanup.\n- pom.xml: remove commented-out require-capability line (Sonar xml:S125).\n- Add JUnit4 + AssertJ tests (15) for NodeStats (incl. the equal-size sibling\n  regression) and the flamegraph writer.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: apply PR-review fixes for correctness, charset safety, and test quality\n\nH1 (blocker): make equals/hashCode use path-only identity in NodeStats.\n  Two nodes with the same JCR path are the same node regardless of size or\n  children; this keeps equals consistent with compareTo''s path tie-break and\n  prevents a TreeSet contract violation (compareTo==0 but equals==false).\n\nH2: replace FileWriter with OutputStreamWriter+UTF_8 at both call sites in\n  ComputeSizeCommand (writeGraphData and writeGraphFooter) so non-ASCII node\n  names on localised sites are never corrupted by the JVM default charset.\n\nM4: change writeGraphNode startPosition parameter from Long to primitive long\n  to eliminate boxing and any NPE risk in the recursive size accumulation.\n\nL1: remove the redundant isDebugEnabled guard around the parameterised\n  LOGGER.debug call; SLF4J evaluates arguments lazily so the guard is noise.\n\nM1: add compareTo_reflexive test to NodeStatsTest.\nM2: tighten startPositionAdvancesAcrossSiblings assertions to full\n  f(level,start,size,0,\"name\") line matches so a wrong-level regression is caught.\nM3: invokeWriteGraphNode helper now declares throws Exception and no longer\n  wraps RepositoryException inside IOException, preserving the original type.\n\nTest: update equals_differentSize_areNotEqual → equals_samePathDifferentSize_areEqual\n  to reflect path-only identity (same path = equal regardless of size).\n\nAll 16 tests pass (NodeStatsTest: 12, ComputeSizeCommandTest: 4).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: address PR review (equals/compareTo consistency, UTF-8 output)\n\n- NodeStats equals/hashCode now key on path only (a node''s identity is its\n  unique JCR path; size and children are derived), making them consistent with\n  compareTo''s tie-break so the TreeSet never collapses distinct nodes\n- ComputeSizeCommand: write the flamegraph via UTF-8 OutputStreamWriter instead\n  of platform-default FileWriter (fixes mojibake for non-ASCII node names);\n  use primitive long for the recursive startPosition; keep the isDebugEnabled\n  guard since the debug arg (byteCountToDisplaySize) is evaluated eagerly\n- Tests: add compareTo reflexivity, full-line assertions for the sibling\n  start-position case, helper no longer erases RepositoryException type\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: manage FileOutputStream as a try-with-resources variable\n\nDeclare the FileOutputStream as its own TWR resource at both flamegraph writer\nsites instead of constructing it inline inside OutputStreamWriter, so it is\nalways closed even if the writer constructor fails (Sonar S2095).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNs5UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ1wQAKGxzr8KW7jgu6QWHYNkn+He\nmTqAz4G0eVlmQuW1ODfcZ2mzKPhVw+wyRgQGPjE5EyDGSE22yARrbPK