ptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hassanzohdy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hassanzohdy/mongez-cache/commits/d33b09ad968cb4f512eaa9abd07036c5728a6367/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-27T13:50:01Z","email":"hassanzohdy@gmail.com","name":"Hasan Zohdy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-27T13:50:01Z","email":"hassanzohdy@gmail.com","name":"Hasan Zohdy"},"message":"docs(skills): pass-2 polish — reconcile 6 drift item(s) with source\n\n- skills/runtime/SKILL.md: drop stale \"known has(missingKey) === true bug\" wording from frontmatter — RunTimeDriver.getItem now returns null on miss (matches Web Storage contract); body already documents the fix.\n- skills/encryption/SKILL.md: drop stale \"known TTL bug\" wording from frontmatter — EncryptedLocalStorageDriver.set now wraps in the {data, expiresAt} envelope before encrypting, so TTL works (already documented in body).\n- skills/local-storage/SKILL.md: corruption recovery wording said the malformed entry is left in place; BaseCacheEngine.get actually calls remove(key) inside the parse catch — corrected to \"removes the malformed entry\".\n- skills/manager/SKILL.md: cache.has table row claimed expiry was checked; BaseCacheEngine.has only checks getItem !== null. Aligned with README/basic-usage voice.\n- skills/manager/SKILL.md: CacheManagerInterface.setDriver was typed as returning CacheManagerInterface; the actual interface in src/types.ts returns void (impl returns this, but the type is void). Aligned with source.\n- skills/custom-drivers/SKILL.md: claim that the encrypted drivers override set/get to \"bypass the envelope\" is no longer true — they wrap in {data, expiresAt} before encrypting so TTL keeps working.\n- skills/recipes/SKILL.md: observable-cache snippet imported a non-existent `EventBus` named export from @mongez/events; the package exports a default `events` instance only. Switched to the default import.\n\nCo-Authore